# Croatian (Hrvatski) — every `@tr("…")` string of the interface.
#
# The `.slint` files are the source of truth: the entries below follow them file
# by file, and a string without an entry falls back to its English source text
# (English is the source language, so `translations/en/` stays empty). Regenerate
# with `slint-tr-extractor --no-default-translation-context` after marking new
# strings — the catalogs are context-free (see crates/ui/build.rs).
#
# Rust backend-formatted UI text is owned by `crates/ui/src/backend_text.rs`.
# Slint's bundled PO catalog is compiled from the `.slint` literals; backend
# formatting uses its Rust API in the same crate because it needs dynamic
# helpers and plural forms.
#
# Register: the interface addresses the user in the formal plural ("vi") —
# "Prikažite…", "Izbrišite…", "Pridružite se". Two labels are deliberately
# shorter than the literal translation so the phone-width rows still fit
# ("Copy link" → "Kopirajte URL", "Create invite" → "Nova pozivnica"); the
# Croatian-width phases in tests/addons/addon_row_fit.rs and
# tests/settings_sync/sync_overflow.rs guard that.
#
# Values that are identifiers in the data rather than prose stay as they are:
# stored category names, addon names, stream/codec labels, `JPEG`/`WebP`,
# `HW+`/`HW`/`SW`, `P2P`, `HLS`/`DASH`, `VLC`, `mpv`, `Stremio`, `Cinemeta`,
# and unit abbreviations (GB / MB / KB).
